<div class="box-example"><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Map:_General_Chemistry_(Petrucci_et_al.)/26:_Structure_of_Organic_Compounds/26.1:_Organic_Compounds_and_Structures:_An_Overview" class="mt-section"><span id="Example_.5C(.5CPageIndex.7B2.7D.5C)"></span><h5 class="box-legend lt-chem-24379 editable"><span class="lt-icon-default">Example \(\PageIndex{2}\)</span></h5>

<p class="lt-chem-24379">Draw the structure for each compound.</p>

<ol>
    <li class="lt-chem-24379">2,3-dimethylbutane</li>
    <li class="lt-chem-24379">4-ethyl-2-methylheptane</li>
</ol>

<p class="simpara lt-chem-24379"><strong>Solution</strong></p>

<p class="lt-chem-24379">In drawing structures, always start with the parent chain.</p>

<ol>
    <li class="lt-chem-24379">The parent chain is butane, indicating four carbon atoms in the LCC.
    <div class="informalfigure large"><img alt="Ex2 1a.jpg" style="width: 600px; height: 46px;" width="600px" height="46px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/27431/Ex2_1a.jpg?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=600&amp;height=46" /></div>

    <p class="lt-chem-24379">Then add the groups at their proper positions. You can number the parent chain from either direction as long as you are consistent; just don&rsquo;t change directions before the structure is done. The name indicates two methyl (CH<sub>3</sub>) groups, one on the second carbon atom and one on the third.</p>

    <div class="informalfigure large"><img alt="Ex2 1b.jpg" style="width: 600px; height: 95px;" width="600px" height="95px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/27433/Ex2_1b.jpg?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=600&amp;height=95" /></div>

    <p class="lt-chem-24379">Finally, fill in all the hydrogen atoms, keeping in mind that each carbon atom must have four bonds.</p>

    <div class="informalfigure large"><img alt="Ex2 1c.jpg" style="width: 600px; height: 86px;" width="600px" height="86px" class="internal" loading="lazy" src="https://chem.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/27435/Ex2_1c.jpg?revision=1&amp;size=bestfit&amp;width=600&amp;height=86" /></div>
    </li>
    <li class="lt-chem-24379">Adding the groups at their proper positions gives

